1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:04,254
<i>I can't forgive you</i>
<i>for what you did to Oliver.</i>

2
00:00:06,214 --> 00:00:07,924
<i>My only request is,</i>

3
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:12,137
<i>if you want to hurt someone for revenge,</i>

4
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:15,265
<i>let it be me, Mariela.</i>

5
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:18,643
[JORDAN] <i>Hey, dude.</i>

6
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,771
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

7
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:24,482
<i>I didn't hear the news right away.</i>

8
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,570
<i>Dude, otherwise, I would've been here.</i>

9
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:30,363
<i>I would've dropped everything.</i>

10
00:00:30,947 --> 00:00:32,657
<i>I heard you paid part of the bill?</i>

11
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:34,659
<i>It's the least I could do for Oliver.</i>

12
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,286
<i>You didn't have to do that.</i>

13
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:39,789
<i>Billy, I just wanted to help.</i>

14
00:00:41,207 --> 00:00:42,959
<i>That's what we do, right?</i>

15
00:00:43,543 --> 00:00:45,795
<i>We help each other out</i>
<i>when things get tough.</i>

16
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:52,260
[PRECIOUS]<i> Why did you</i>
<i>bring that woman here?</i>

17
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:54,929
[ENRICO] <i>She wanted to visit Oliver.</i>

18
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,848
<i>But Billy was here,</i>

19
00:00:56,931 --> 00:00:59,434
<i>so I just sent her home</i>
<i>to avoid any trouble.</i>

20
00:00:59,517 --> 00:01:01,519
[PRECIOUS] <i>Of course there'd be trouble.</i>

21
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:03,271
<i>You shouldn't have brought her here.</i>

22
00:01:04,355 --> 00:01:06,941
<i>She tried to save Oliver's life.</i>

23
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:09,944
<i>She even got stabbed herself, remember?</i>

24
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:11,362
<i>Precious…</i>

25
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,948
<i>Bea's changed.</i>

26
00:01:14,908 --> 00:01:16,826
<i>I'm sure of that.</i>

27
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:18,661
<i>Well, it's too late.</i>

28
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:22,082
<i>Billy won't forgive her again.</i>

29
00:01:22,749 --> 00:01:24,959
<i>She wants to put Bea back in prison.</i>

30
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:29,422
<i>Do you think I'm only doing this for Bea?</i>

31
00:01:29,506 --> 00:01:32,258
<i>I'm also doing this for Billy.</i>

32
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:35,720
<i>I don't want her</i>
<i>to be consumed by her anger,</i>

33
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:37,722
<i>just like Bea was before.</i>

34
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:43,520
[ROBBIE]<i> Family problems</i>
<i>are the worst, man.</i>

35
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:44,813
<i>They hurt more.</i>

36
00:01:46,064 --> 00:01:47,398
<i>Just like with me and Dad.</i>

37
00:01:48,024 --> 00:01:49,400
[ROBBIE] <i>Where could he be?</i>

38
00:01:53,696 --> 00:01:55,031
<i>Man, I should've listened to Billy.</i>

39
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:56,491
<i>I should've had him arrested.</i>

40
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:59,577
<i>I shouldn't feel bad</i>
<i>or give him another chance.</i>

41
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:01,746
<i>He hasn't changed at all.</i>

42
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,248
<i>He's still a criminal.</i>

43
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:04,582
[ROBBIE] <i>Let's go back inside?</i>

44
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,501
<i>You should sing again.</i>

45
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:21,850
[EKG MACHINE BEEPING]

46
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:31,442
The doctor said

47
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:35,989
Oliver can soon be transferred
to a regular room.

48
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:41,911
His condition and vital signs
are getting more stable.

49
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:46,166
Even if he recovers,
I'm not going to accept Bea.

50
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:50,378
Billy, Bea has learned her lesson.

51
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:52,547
Can't you give her a chance?

52
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:53,673
Are you blind?!

53
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:57,010
After everything that happened,
you still think she's innocent?

54
00:02:57,093 --> 00:02:59,220
What more do you want?!

55
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:03,057
You're trying to force your children to
get along when you know it's impossible.

56
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:08,813
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

57
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:20,950
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

58
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:25,848
[EKG MACHINE BEEPING]

59
00:04:42,782 --> 00:04:44,075
Billy?

60
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:46,911
Hi.

61
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:48,913
Hi, Oliver!

62
00:04:49,872 --> 00:04:51,124
Hello!

63
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:53,918
[BILLY SNIFFLES]

64
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:56,504
How do you feel?

65
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:00,133
Does it hurt here? [SNIFFLES]

66
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:06,431
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

67
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:09,350
Is Mariela gone?

68
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:11,352
She's gone. You're safe now.

69
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:16,065
She's back in jail,
and she won't hurt you anymore.

70
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:18,359
She can't get near you again.

71
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,361
Same with Bea.

72
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:23,614
Bea can't hurt you anymore.

73
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:27,452
- [BILLY SNIFFLES]
- Where is Bea?

74
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:31,456
She saved my life.

75
00:05:33,082 --> 00:05:36,294
Bea won't hurt me.

76
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:40,923
I saw how she got stabbed, Billy.

77
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:46,971
[SOBBING SOFTLY]

78
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:54,062
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

79
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:02,361
I'm back.

80
00:06:03,404 --> 00:06:06,324
- [PLATES CLINKING]
- Take a break. Eat this first.

81
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:12,038
Where did you get the money to buy that?

82
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:14,415
Some unpaid debts.

83
00:06:15,374 --> 00:06:18,961
There you go again!
You haven't changed at all!

84
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:20,338
What's your problem?

85
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:24,425
You think I can get a decent job?
I'm a fugitive!

86
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:27,470
You're a fugitive, not an idiot!

87
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:29,013
- Keep your mouth--
- Do it!

88
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:32,433
Hurt me again,
and I'll leave you for good!

89
00:06:32,517 --> 00:06:34,393
- You can't do it.
- I can.

90
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:37,980
I'm not like your martyr wife

91
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:40,441
who spent years suffering with you.

92
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:43,444
<i>Silly you!</i>

93
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:48,032
- [DINO WHISPERING]
<i>- Such a smooth talker.</i>

94
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:51,035
[CLEARS THROAT]

95
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:56,958
<i>Jade.</i>

96
00:06:57,583 --> 00:06:59,502
<i>Jade, wait. Um…</i>

97
00:07:01,003 --> 00:07:02,380
<i>I'm sorry. Don't be angry.</i>

98
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:03,965
<i>She's just my friend.</i>

99
00:07:04,048 --> 00:07:06,050
<i>Don't come home to us.</i>

100
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:08,261
[DINO] <i>What are you talking about?</i>

101
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:10,179
<i>Are you like this because</i>
<i>you're the breadwinner?</i>

102
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:14,350
<i>Yes! You're using my money</i>
<i>to flirt with your mistress!</i>

103
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:16,102
<i>Now you're talking to me like that?!</i>

104
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:18,020
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>Hey! No!</i>

105
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:25,987
So please, for the sake of our baby,

106
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:28,489
change your ways, okay?

107
00:07:28,573 --> 00:07:31,117
All we need is some capital
to start a business.

108
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:33,119
Why don't you ask Jordan?

109
00:07:33,202 --> 00:07:36,289
I'm trying, okay?
But it's even harder now.

110
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:38,541
His friend keeps telling him
to get rid of me!

111
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:40,460
Which friend?

112
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:47,925
What time will you finish work?

113
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:51,095
[ENRICO] <i>I'm just waiting for</i>
<i>the supplies to be delivered.</i>

114
00:07:51,179 --> 00:07:52,847
After that, I'll go there.

115
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:54,807
Do you want me to bring anything?

116
00:07:54,891 --> 00:07:57,977
[OLIVER] Is it possible
for you to bring Bea over?

117
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:02,064
I just want to thank her, Pa.

118
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:04,942
Because she saved my life.

119
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:09,322
What are you doing?

120
00:08:10,865 --> 00:08:13,784
You've been on your phone
for hours. You need rest.

121
00:08:20,124 --> 00:08:21,083
Here.

122
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:25,963
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

123
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:29,008
Drink this. Then go to sleep.

124
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:42,021
Billy.

125
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:48,986
[UTENSILS, PLATES CLINKING]

126
00:08:53,658 --> 00:08:55,785
Your father called.

127
00:08:57,370 --> 00:09:00,831
Your father said Oliver wants to see Bea.

128
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:05,211
Billy, just try to understand
your brother.

129
00:09:05,294 --> 00:09:08,422
He saw how Bea protected him.

130
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:15,680
Don't tell me
you're going soft on her too.

131
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:18,558
I was just thinking, Billy.

132
00:09:18,641 --> 00:09:22,562
If Bea really did all that
for Oliver, maybe…

133
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:26,148
maybe she really has changed.

134
00:09:29,026 --> 00:09:31,404
What's going on with all of you?

135
00:09:31,487 --> 00:09:34,824
Billy, it's not good to live with anger.

136
00:09:35,449 --> 00:09:37,827
Maybe forgiveness can
give you a fresh start.

137
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,955
Do you know that Bea has a new lawyer?

138
00:09:42,206 --> 00:09:45,585
She couldn't have gotten one without Dad.

139
00:09:45,668 --> 00:09:48,462
Why is he helping that criminal?

140
00:09:49,463 --> 00:09:53,926
Billy, if you think Enrico is
taking sides, you're mistaken.

141
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:56,053
He's just being a father to you three.

142
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,097
Billy.

143
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:03,978
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

144
00:10:19,035 --> 00:10:20,328
LET'S STOP USING LOVELIST!

145
00:10:20,411 --> 00:10:22,288
FORGET THE USERS.
THE CEO IS THE MAIN CHARACTER.

146
00:10:22,371 --> 00:10:23,831
AREN'T YOU TIRED OF YOUR CEO'S ISSUES?

147
00:10:23,914 --> 00:10:26,208
- NEW ENTRY. HER BROTHER WAS STABBED!
- POOR BOY.

148
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:28,294
HACKING, FIRE, COURT DRAMA…
NOW, STABBING?

149
00:10:28,377 --> 00:10:33,591
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

150
00:10:53,903 --> 00:10:55,863
ANOTHER ISSUE AGAIN? OH MY.

151
00:10:55,946 --> 00:10:58,115
THE CEO IS THE APP'S MAIN CHARACTER,
NOT THE USERS.

152
00:10:58,199 --> 00:11:01,077
THIS IS A SERIOUS INCIDENT, BUT IT DOESN'T
ERASE THE ISSUES WITH YOUR LEADERSHIP.

153
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:06,374
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

154
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:09,502
- SO MANY ISSUES. WHAT IS HAPPENING?
- I THINK SHE DESERVES IT HAHA OOPS

155
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:12,713
CAN WE TALK ABOUT THE ACTUAL ISSUES
INSTEAD OF MAKING ANOTHER EXCUSE?

156
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:14,715
- TIME TO UNINSTALL LOVELIST!
- NO TO LOVELIST

157
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:17,551
AT THIS POINT, THE CEO IS THE MAIN
CHARACTER OF THE APP, NOT USERS.

158
00:11:17,635 --> 00:11:20,179
[CHUCKLES] Okay. If you say so.

159
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:23,557
I'M SKEPTICAL. HOW CAN YOU EXPECT
USERS TO TRUST YOU?

160
00:11:23,641 --> 00:11:29,397
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,857
- ANOTHER DAY, ANOTHER ISSUE?
- LOVELIST IS GOING DOWN!

162
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:35,111
TOO BAD. I WAS ALMOST IMPRESSED.
BOO, LOVELIST!

163
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:37,029
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

164
00:11:44,912 --> 00:11:46,455
CEO, CAN YOU GIVE US A BREAK, PLEASE?

165
00:11:46,539 --> 00:11:48,958
IT'S JUST A PUBLICITY GIMMICK.
I HEARD LOVELIST IS GOING BANKRUPT.

166
00:11:49,041 --> 00:11:51,377
I THINK YOU'RE THE COMPANY'S
BIGGEST PROBLEM.

167
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:53,921
IS BILLY THE ONE REPLYING TO
THE COMMENTS? SO CHEAP!

168
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:59,844
THIS IS WHAT YOU ALL WANT, RIGHT?

169
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:07,268
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

170
00:12:09,603 --> 00:12:11,021
[GLASS THUDS]

171
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:15,234
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

172
00:12:17,194 --> 00:12:18,571
[ANGRY SHOUT]

173
00:12:22,199 --> 00:12:28,080
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

174
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:38,382
[SOBBING]

175
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:40,259
[ANGRY SHOUT]

176
00:12:40,342 --> 00:12:45,681
- [GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [SOBBING, BREATHING HEAVILY]

177
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:52,104
[CHARM] Toni, it's final.

178
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:54,356
Jimenez Jewelers
decided not to renew their contract

179
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,900
for ad placement.

180
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:57,568
And also Tulips Manila.

181
00:12:57,651 --> 00:13:00,571
And as I speak, three more
of our advertisers

182
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:03,199
have expressed intent
to pull out their ads.

183
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:08,579
Okay, so I guess it's not the time
for me to present my projection

184
00:13:08,662 --> 00:13:11,332
and recommendations for the next quarter.

185
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:13,417
I'm not going to present it to Billy yet.

186
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:15,002
[CHARM] Yeah, don't.

187
00:13:15,085 --> 00:13:16,295
[TONI SIGHS SHARPLY]

188
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:21,717
No, Toni.

189
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:24,303
Go, proceed.

190
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:29,391
I hate to say this, Billy, but…

191
00:13:30,392 --> 00:13:33,854
I think we need to lay off
some of our employees.

192
00:13:33,938 --> 00:13:36,649
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

193
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:39,068
I'm sorry, Billy, but if we don't do that,

194
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:41,987
the company will continue
to bleed financially.

195
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:46,534
I'm looking around this room,

196
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:51,080
and seeing some of the smartest people
in the company.

197
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:54,750
And you're telling me
that's your suggestion?

198
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:57,795
A layoff?

199
00:14:00,631 --> 00:14:03,759
Am I the only one
thinking of solutions here?

200
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:07,346
Help me, will you?

201
00:14:07,429 --> 00:14:11,016
But, chief, this is one of
the solutions I can think of.

202
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:13,894
One of the solutions,
but not the only one, Toni!

203
00:14:13,978 --> 00:14:15,896
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:19,108
The company pays us to think.

205
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,028
Show some concern for our employees.

206
00:14:23,112 --> 00:14:29,201
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

207
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:36,750
All good now, sir.

208
00:14:38,627 --> 00:14:40,421
- Miss, my computer hung.
- Oh.

209
00:14:42,089 --> 00:14:44,383
Let me check.

210
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:48,554
- There you go.
- Perfect! Thank you, miss.

211
00:14:48,637 --> 00:14:49,930
Bea.

212
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:51,223
- Sir.
- Good job.

213
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:53,142
- [BEA] Thank you.
- Anyway…

214
00:14:53,225 --> 00:14:54,810
Here's your salary advance.

215
00:14:56,353 --> 00:14:57,605
Sir, thank you.

216
00:14:57,688 --> 00:14:58,939
Don't mention it.

217
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:05,613
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

218
00:15:05,696 --> 00:15:09,992
<i>Gosh, what's this,</i>
<i>LoveList CEO Billy Cariño?</i>

219
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:11,785
<i>Trauma marketing?</i>

220
00:15:11,869 --> 00:15:13,454
<i>That's so cheap!</i>

221
00:15:13,537 --> 00:15:16,206
<i>You're always full of negative vibes.</i>

222
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:18,918
<i>- It's like you have an unlimited supply.</i>
- [UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

223
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:21,253
<i>This is Jordan's friend</i>
<i>you were talking about?</i>

224
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:23,547
<i>Billy Cariño, the CEO of LoveList?</i>

225
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:24,965
- [DINO HUFFS]
- Here, look.

226
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:27,927
[DINO] So, she's a CEO, huh?
She must be loaded.

227
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:30,846
[KAREN] That woman is full of negativity.

228
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:33,057
Good thing it didn't rub off on Jordan.

229
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,352
Your son is doing great, actually.

230
00:15:36,435 --> 00:15:39,396
He got more famous
after what happened to Caloy.

231
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:41,690
[VLOGGER] <i>From being an ordinary person</i>

232
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:45,235
<i>to OMG status in just</i>
<i>over a month. </i>[CHUCKLES]

233
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:46,946
<i>That's Jordan, guys.</i>

234
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:49,073
<i>He's been in the news again recently</i>

235
00:15:49,156 --> 00:15:51,492
<i>because he's one of the reasons why</i>

236
00:15:51,575 --> 00:15:55,579
<i>Carlos Toledo, a wanted criminal, is gone.</i>

237
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:58,874
<i>As in, no more.</i>
[CHUCKLES]

238
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,168
<i>One less bad person in this world.</i>

239
00:16:01,251 --> 00:16:04,296
<i>Like, Jordan is so perfect, right?</i>

240
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:06,715
<i>He's both a singer and a hero.</i>

241
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:11,387
<i>And, of course,</i>
<i>the fangirl in me got obsessed.</i>

242
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:14,056
<i>Like, who is Jordan really?</i>

243
00:16:14,139 --> 00:16:16,725
<i>So, I did a little bit of research,</i>

244
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:18,686
<i>and voilà!</i>

245
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:21,855
<i>I found his childhood photos.</i>

246
00:16:21,939 --> 00:16:25,526
<i>And guys, when I tell you</i>
<i>that he was cute,</i>

247
00:16:25,609 --> 00:16:28,570
<i>yes, he was really cute!</i>

248
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:29,989
<i>Look.</i>

249
00:16:30,572 --> 00:16:31,865
Is that Billy?

250
00:16:31,949 --> 00:16:33,367
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

251
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:34,910
[DINO] So what if it is?

252
00:16:35,744 --> 00:16:39,164
I think I've seen her as a kid.

253
00:16:40,082 --> 00:16:41,125
Where?

254
00:16:43,919 --> 00:16:45,254
I don't remember.

255
00:16:45,337 --> 00:16:48,424
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:50,092
- [MUSIC FADES]
- [BIRDS CHIRPING]

257
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:54,555
LOVELIST AGAIN?
THAT DATING APP IS CURSED!

258
00:16:54,638 --> 00:16:57,975
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

259
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:14,658
So, is that really the last price?

260
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:17,286
You already asked for
a lower price earlier, right?

261
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:18,787
How much lower do you want?

262
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:20,914
Seriously? 800,000 pesos?

263
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:22,458
I'll take it for 400,000 pesos.

264
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:24,501
That's way too low.

265
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:26,378
I can't sell it for that price.

266
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:27,796
It's low?

267
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,548
This car already has dents.

268
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:32,259
And it has been repainted, right?

269
00:17:32,342 --> 00:17:35,888
[SCOFFS] Besides, this isn't
a high-end car.

270
00:17:36,638 --> 00:17:37,639
Well?

271
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:40,434
At least it's maintained better
than your attitude.

272
00:17:40,517 --> 00:17:42,102
- What?
- Nothing.

273
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:43,979
800,000 pesos. Take it or leave it.

274
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:48,150
Good luck finding someone
who'll buy that car!

275
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,112
Fine, suit yourself!

276
00:17:54,406 --> 00:17:59,411
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:02,122
[FRUSTRATED SCREAM]

278
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:07,086
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

279
00:18:18,305 --> 00:18:20,099
[BEA] <i>I thought of gifting it to you.</i>

280
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:24,144
[OLIVER] <i>Thank you, Bea.</i>
<i>I love you so, so, so much!</i>

281
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:25,687
[BEA] <i>Wow! You love me</i>
<i>just because of that?</i>

282
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:27,356
- [PRECIOUS CHUCKLES]
<i>- </i>[OLIVER] <i>Thank you.</i>

283
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:29,399
- [BEA] <i>Welcome.</i>
- [OLIVER]<i> I love you.</i>

284
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:32,194
<i>- Seriously?</i>
<i>- Uh…</i>

285
00:18:32,277 --> 00:18:33,612
<i>- You're unbelievable!</i>
<i>- Billy.</i>

286
00:18:33,695 --> 00:18:35,989
<i>- You've got some nerve!</i>
<i>- Billy! Billy!</i>

287
00:18:36,073 --> 00:18:38,283
<i>- Leave my brother alone!</i>
<i>- Stay there, Oliver.</i>

288
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:40,119
<i>- How dare you come here?!</i>
<i>- Billy, stop!</i>

289
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:41,870
<i>- What else do you want, huh?!</i>
<i>- Billy. Billy!</i>

290
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:43,747
<i>- Get out! Leave!</i>
<i>- Billy!</i>

291
00:18:43,831 --> 00:18:46,125
<i>Don't ever come back here! Get out!</i>

292
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:48,127
<i>- I have no bad intentions.</i>
<i>- Billy!</i>

293
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:49,920
<i>Oliver, stay away from her.</i>

294
00:18:50,003 --> 00:18:51,004
<i>I said stay away from her!</i>

295
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:53,507
<i>She's not doing anything wrong to you.</i>

296
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:54,758
<i>I'm just protecting you.</i>

297
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:56,802
<i>Listen to me. I'm your sister, aren't I?</i>

298
00:18:56,885 --> 00:18:58,470
<i>Come here now.</i>

299
00:18:58,554 --> 00:18:59,847
<i>- I said come here!</i>
<i>- Billy!</i>

300
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:00,973
<i>- She's a bad person!</i>
<i>- Billy!</i>

301
00:19:01,056 --> 00:19:02,182
<i>- Stay away from her!</i>
<i>- Billy!</i>

302
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:03,600
<i>- Come here!</i>
<i>- I don't want to!</i>

303
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:05,227
<i>Stop! You're hurting Oliver!</i>

304
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:07,146
<i>Come here.</i>

305
00:19:07,229 --> 00:19:09,690
<i>You're the one turning into</i>
<i>a bad person, Billy.</i>

306
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:11,650
<i>Oh, really?!</i>

307
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:13,902
<i>Stay away from Billy for now.</i>

308
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:15,279
<i>Just leave them be.</i>

309
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:17,364
<i>No, Pa.</i>

310
00:19:18,073 --> 00:19:19,533
<i>I'll keep trying.</i>

311
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:21,827
<i>I won't give up.</i>

312
00:19:21,910 --> 00:19:24,788
<i>I won't get tired of trying</i>
<i>even if it's difficult.</i>

313
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:27,457
<i>The lawyer said</i>

314
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:29,751
<i>there's a chance you won't</i>
<i>be held accountable.</i>

315
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:32,171
<i>It's not about that anymore.</i>

316
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:35,007
<i>I admit, I tried to put on an act before</i>

317
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:37,968
<i>so that I could get acquitted.</i>

318
00:19:38,635 --> 00:19:41,889
<i>But now, all I want</i>

319
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:45,100
<i>is Billy's forgiveness.</i>

320
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:47,561
<i>Where's Valerie? Where is she?</i>

321
00:19:47,644 --> 00:19:49,563
<i>She said she won't come today.</i>

322
00:19:49,646 --> 00:19:53,233
<i>She's meeting with a client</i>
<i>who wants to be Jordan's sponsor.</i>

323
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:54,776
<i>Wow!</i>

324
00:19:55,527 --> 00:19:57,988
<i>She found a sponsor for Jordan, huh?</i>

325
00:19:58,071 --> 00:19:59,448
<i>Good for her.</i>

326
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:01,909
<i>What about you, Marj? Tell me.</i>

327
00:20:01,992 --> 00:20:04,786
<i>Are you even working?</i>
<i>Can you still do your job?</i>

328
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:08,457
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

329
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:10,167
<i>I want you to find replacements</i>

330
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:12,461
<i>for those advertisers who pulled out.</i>

331
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:14,463
<i>I don't care how you're gonna do it.</i>

332
00:20:14,546 --> 00:20:17,424
<i>I just want results</i>
<i>by tomorrow on my table!</i>

333
00:20:17,507 --> 00:20:20,636
<i>Billy was the one who hit Jade with a car!</i>

334
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:26,642
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

335
00:20:26,725 --> 00:20:30,270
<i>Then I saw her again at the wake.</i>

336
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:33,190
<i>I guess she went there</i>
<i>because she was feeling guilty.</i>

337
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:35,651
<i>Dino.</i>

338
00:20:35,734 --> 00:20:40,405
<i>Billy was the one</i>
<i>driving the car that hit Jade.</i>

339
00:20:41,406 --> 00:20:43,116
<i>I'm sure it was Billy.</i>

340
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:45,118
<i>Billy was the one who killed Jade.</i>

341
00:20:45,202 --> 00:20:48,330
[SCREAMS]

342
00:20:48,413 --> 00:20:54,836
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]
